    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0460" n="1194" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1194"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Muruaga.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reply to your note of the 30th
                    ultimo, stating that you were advised by the consul of Spain at New Orleans that
                    volunteers were being publicly recruited in that city for the purpose of
                    carrying on hostilities in Cuba against the Government of Spain, I have the
                    honor to say that this Department is in receipt of a letter from the
                    Attorney-General, dated to-day, announcing that the United States district
                    attorney at New Orleans has so far failed to discover any basis for the
                    representations contained in your note above referred to. He will, however,
                    continue his investigation of the charge.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
